Model weights
  The WorldCast generator weights are fine-tuned from Wan2.2-TI2V-5B
  (https://huggingface.co/Wan-AI/Wan2.2-TI2V-5B, revision 921dbaf3f1674a56f47e83fb80a34bac8a8f203e),
  Apache License 2.0, by the WorldCast authors. The Wan2.2 VAE and the umT5-XXL text encoder
  (google/umt5-xxl, Apache License 2.0) are used unmodified. The other weights of the paper's
  metrics are not redistributed: tools/download_weights.py fetches them from where each is
  published. The player detector is fine-tuned from Ultralytics YOLO11x by the WorldCast authors
  and is AGPL-3.0, unlike the other files of the WorldCast weights repository it is published in
  (https://huggingface.co/ZiyangYe/WorldCast, detector/yolo11x_cs2_player.pt); the ultralytics
  package it needs is not distributed with WorldCast.

Data
  Trained and evaluated on the OpenCS2 dataset
  (https://huggingface.co/datasets/blanchon/opencs2_dataset), CC BY 4.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Data files in this release derived from OpenCS2
  (latents, labels, indices) were produced by the WorldCast authors: latents encoded with the
  Wan2.2 VAE, labels computed from the recordings, and round indices. The example cases
  (https://huggingface.co/ZiyangYe/WorldCast) and the evaluation data
  (https://huggingface.co/datasets/ZiyangYe/WorldCast-data) also redistribute OpenCS2's tick tables
  of their rounds under CC BY 4.0.

